---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

        <meta
            name="description"
            content="Explore living aquatic ecosystems designed and built by Microcosmos Atelier."
        />

        <title>Our Work — Microcosmos Atelier</title>
    </head>

    <body>
        <!-- =====================================================
             HEADER
             ===================================================== -->

        <header class="page-header">
            <nav class="nav">
                <a href="/en/" class="logo">Microcosmos Atelier</a>

                <div class="navigation">
                    <a href="/en/our-work">Our Work</a>
                    <a href="/en/about">About</a>
                    <a href="/en/contact">Contact</a>

                    <div class="language-switcher">
                        <a href="/our-work">NL</a>
                        <span>·</span>
                        <a href="/en/" class="active">EN</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </nav>
        </header>

        <main>
            <!-- =====================================================
                 INTRO
                 ===================================================== -->

            <section class="page-intro work-page-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Work</p>

                <h1>
                    Real ecosystems.<br />
                    Actually built.
                </h1>

                <p class="page-intro-text">
                    Each Microcosmos is a collaboration between a space, an idea
                    and a living ecosystem. These are some of the worlds I've
                    created so far.
                </p>
            </section>

            <!-- =====================================================
                 FALLEN FOREST
                 ===================================================== -->

            <article class="case-study">
                <div class="case-study-hero case-study-hero-contain">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A002-05.jpeg"
                        alt="Fallen Forest Microcosmos"
                    />
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">01 — Fallen Forest</p>

                        <h2>
                            A forest floor,<br />
                            brought underwater.
                        </h2>
                    </div>

                    <p class="case-study-intro">
                        For this multifunctional family space,I designed a
                        two-metre-long, 1,000-litre living ecosystem inspired by
                        fallen trees and the dense vegetation that develops
                        around them.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-body">
                    <div class="case-study-story">
                        <p>
                            Rather than recreating a particular biotope, this
                            Microcosmos takes inspiration from the structure of
                            a fallen tree in a tropical forest — the open spaces
                            between branches, the layers of vegetation, and the
                            life that gathers around decaying organic matter.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Large groups of lemon tetras, emperor tetras and
                            hatchetfish bring movement to the open water, each
                            occupying a different part of the water column.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The tetras move through the central spaces between
                            the branches and vegetation, while the hatchetfish
                            remain close to the surface. Corydoras constantly
                            explore the lower layers, sifting through leaf
                            litter and substrate in search of food.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Above the water, Monstera and Pothos grow out of the
                            aquarium, drawing nutrients directly from the water.
                            Shrimp, snails and microorganisms occupy the less
                            visible layers of the ecosystem, processing organic
                            matter and contributing to the system's nutrient
                            cycles.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The result is not a static composition, but a living
                            system that continues to change as the plants grow,
                            populations develop and the ecosystem matures.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <aside class="ecosystem-details">
                        <p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem</p>

                        <div class="ecosystem-principle">
                            <p>
                                This Microcosmos is designed around the
                                ecological structure of a fallen tree in a
                                tropical forest — where decaying wood, leaf
                                litter, vegetation and water create a network of
                                interconnected habitats.
                            </p>

                            <p>
                                Different organisms occupy different layers of
                                the system, from fish moving through the open
                                water to Corydoras exploring the substrate and
                                shrimp, snails and microorganisms processing
                                organic matter below the surface.
                            </p>

                            <p>
                                The system is deliberately given time to mature.
                                Plants grow, microorganisms establish themselves
                                and the relationships between its inhabitants
                                gradually develop into a more stable and
                                balanced ecosystem.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="details-grid">
                            <div>
                                <span>Established</span>
                                <strong>May 2023</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Dimensions</span>
                                <strong>200 × 65 × 75 cm</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Volume</span>
                                <strong>1,000 L</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Filtration</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Internal · pumice-based substrate
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Lighting</span>
                                <strong> 2 photoperiods · 6 h + 4 h </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Substraat</span>
                                <strong>MA-Gen 1.0</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>CO₂</span>
                                <strong> 2 bpm during photoperiod </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Fish</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Hyphessobrycon pulchripinnis ·
                                    Hyphessobrycon sweglesi · Nematobrycon
                                    palmeri · Carnegiella strigata · Corydoras
                                    elegans · Crossocheilus oblongus
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Other inhabitants</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Amano shrimp · Neocaridina · snails ·
                                    microfauna
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Plants</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Echinodorus uruguayensis · Cryptocoryne
                                    wendtii · Cryptocoryne undulata · Hygrophila
                                    stricta · Bolbitis heudelotii
                                </strong>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </aside>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-gallery">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A002-02.jpeg"
                        alt="Fallen Forest Microcosmos detail"
                    />

                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A002-01.jpeg"
                        alt="Fallen Forest Microcosmos detail"
                    />
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- =====================================================
                 ORINOCO / LITTORAL
                 ===================================================== -->

            <article class="case-study">
                <div class="case-study-hero">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A003-06.jpeg"
                        alt="Orinoco-inspired littoral Microcosmos"
                    />
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">
                            02 — Orinoco-inspired littoral zone
                        </p>

                        <h2>
                            Where land<br />
                            meets water.
                        </h2>
                    </div>

                    <p class="case-study-intro">
                        A carefully composed interpretation of the shallow
                        shores of the Orinoco basin, where land, water and
                        vegetation come together.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-body">
                    <div class="case-study-story">
                        <p>
                            Inspired by the quiet, tannin-rich waters of the
                            Orinoco basin, this Microcosmos brings a fragment of
                            the transition between land and water indoors.
                            Long-leaved aquatic plants, riparian vegetation,
                            fallen leaves and wood create a layered landscape
                            where water and land seem to flow into one another.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            In the open water, <em>Nannostomus marginatus</em> move
                            gently among the vegetation. Their characteristic, almost
                            weightless posture brings life to the upper layers of
                            the aquarium. Closer to the substrate, <em
                                >Apistogramma viejita</em
                            > explore the spaces between leaves and wood, constantly
                            investigating their surroundings and sifting through the
                            fine substrate for food.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Between these layers, <em>Ancistrus</em> slowly move across
                            wood, leaves and plants. Together, the inhabitants are
                            not simply a collection of individual species, but a community
                            in which each animal occupies its own place and follows
                            its own rhythm.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The result is an aquarium that does more than
                            reference a river landscape. It seeks to capture its
                            atmosphere: warm, quiet and constantly alive.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <aside class="ecosystem-details">
                        <p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem</p>

                        <div class="details-grid">
                            <div>
                                <span>Established</span>
                                <strong>August 2025</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Dimensions</span>
                                <strong>72 × 60 × 60 cm</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Volume</span>
                                <strong>220 L</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Filtration</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Internal · pumice-based substrate
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Lighting</span>
                                <strong
                                    >LED · 2 light periods · 6 h + 4 h</strong
                                >
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Substraat</span>
                                <strong>mainly sand, MA-Gen 1.0</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>CO₂</span>
                                <strong>-</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Fish</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Nannostomus marginatus · Apistogramma
                                    viejita · Ancistrus brown
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Other inhabitants</span>
                                <strong> Snails · microfauna </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Plants</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Echinodorus bleheri · Eleocharis acicularis
                                </strong>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </aside>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-gallery">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A003-01.jpeg"
                        alt="Detail of Orinoco-inspired Microcosmos"
                    />

                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A003-03.jpeg"
                        alt="Detail of Orinoco-inspired Microcosmos"
                    />

                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A003-04.jpeg"
                        alt="Detail of Orinoco-inspired Microcosmos"
                    />
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- =====================================================
                 BORNEO UNDERSTORY
                 ===================================================== -->

            <article class="case-study">
                <div class="case-study-hero">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A004-01.jpeg"
                        alt="Borneo Understory Microcosmos"
                    />
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">03 — Borneo Understory</p>

                        <h2>
                            A forest<br />
                            beneath the water.
                        </h2>
                    </div>

                    <p class="case-study-intro">
                        A small living ecosystem inspired by the forest floor
                        and shallow waters of Borneo.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-body">
                    <div class="case-study-story">
                        <p>
                            A network of fallen branches and roots creates a
                            dense three-dimensional structure, while
                            Cryptocoryne and other low-growing plants emerge
                            from the sandy substrate, giving the aquarium the
                            character of a submerged forest understory.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Rather than recreating a specific location, the
                            design captures the atmosphere and ecological
                            structure of Borneo's tropical forests: shaded,
                            humid and densely layered.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Small groups of Chili Rasboras move quietly between
                            the branches and vegetation, while blue shrimp
                            explore the wood, leaves and substrate, grazing on
                            biofilm and microorganisms.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Over time, the wood, plants and microfauna become
                            increasingly interconnected, allowing the aquarium
                            to develop its own small-scale ecology.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <aside class="ecosystem-details">
                        <div class="details-grid">
                            <div>
                                <span>Established</span>
                                <strong>August 2026</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Dimensions</span>
                                <strong>40 × 40 × 40 cm</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Volume</span>
                                <strong>60 L</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Filtration</span>
                                <strong> Internal · sponge </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Lighting</span>
                                <strong> 10 hour photoperiod </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Substrate</span>
                                <strong>MA-Gen 2.0</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>CO₂</span>
                                <strong>-</strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Fish</span>
                                <strong> Chili Rasbora </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Other inhabitants</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Neocaridina blue · microfauna 
                                </strong>
                            </div>

                            <div>
                                <span>Plants</span>
                                <strong>
                                    Cryptocoryne wendtii (green, red and brown)
                                    · Cryptocoryne undulata · Cryptocoryne
                                    beckettii · Cryptocoryne lucens ·
                                    Cryptocoryne parva · Cryptocoryne petchii ·
                                    Sagittaria subulata · Bolbitis heudelotii
                                </strong>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </aside>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-gallery">
                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A004-02.jpeg"
                        alt="Borneo Understory Microcosmos detail"
                    />

                    <img
                        src="/images/our-work/A004-03.jpeg"
                        alt="Borneo Understory Microcosmos detail"
                    />
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- =====================================================
                 CLOSING
                 ===================================================== -->

            <section class="work-closing">
                <p class="eyebrow">Your space</p>

                <h2>
                    Perhaps the next<br />
                    one is yours.
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Every project is different. If you have a space, an idea, or
                    simply a fascination with aquatic ecosystems, let's start
                    there.
                </p>

                <a href="/en/contact" class="button dark-button">
                    Start a conversation
                </a>
            </section>
        </main>

        <!-- =====================================================
             FOOTER
             ===================================================== -->

        <footer>
            <p>
                © {new Date().getFullYear()} Microcosmos Atelier
            </p>
        </footer>
    </body>
</html>
